  "note": "Annual election of one-third of the Donaghadee Urban Council, polled Monday 16 January 1928 (Belfast News-Letter, 17 January 1928, p. 7). Eight candidates for four seats; register 1,300, 906 voted, 5 spoiled papers. Morrison was the only one of the three retiring members who stood to be re-elected."
